---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Background, how I work, and the role I'm looking for."
>
  <section class="wrap py-20">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,3.5rem)]">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-measure mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      <p>
        I&rsquo;m a data scientist turned AI engineer in Salt Lake City. From 2022 to early 2026 I
        worked at Strider Technologies, building the pipelines that matched hundreds of millions of
        company records across business registries, trade data and multilingual sources.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work I&rsquo;m proudest of came with a number attached. Sending the uncertain matches
        to a language model for review lifted recall from 71% to 83% and precision from 86% to
        90%. A retrieval model I built to match technical expertise to people reached 97.5% recall
        in its top 20 results. I also built the bias tests an AI resume-screening model had to
        pass before wider use.
      </p>
      <p>
        I studied economics at Brigham Young University, and it is still how I approach a problem:
        what decision is being made, who is making it, and what would change their mind.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since then I have been building on my own: a live photo restoration product, a cooking app
        my wife and I use every week, a research paper on layoffs and new business formation, and
        a case study on who should own a precision-farming machine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-20 grid gap-12 rounded-2xl bg-surface-alt p-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr] sm:p-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)]">How I work</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Start from the customer&rsquo;s decision.</strong> The useful
          question is rarely &ldquo;can a model do this?&rdquo; It is what someone is trying to
          decide, and what evidence would settle it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Set the test first, then report what it says.</strong> I fix
          how a result will be judged before I run it. If the answer goes against my idea, that
          goes in the write-up too.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Ship the smallest real version.</strong> Most projects that
          sound like they need a large system need a smaller one in front of users sooner. Real
          usage answers questions that planning cannot.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Let agents type; keep the judgement.</strong> I build with AI
          coding agents every day. They are fast at writing code and poor at knowing whether it
          answers the right question, so that part stays with me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-20 grid gap-12 border-t border-line pt-14 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)]">What I&rsquo;m looking for</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          I&rsquo;m looking for a forward-deployed or AI engineering role. I do my best work close
          to the person with the problem, while the question is still fuzzy and someone has to
          work out what is worth building.
        </p>
        <p>
          I would like to do that on a team that cares whether the thing still works after the
          demo.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:tanner.kunz22@gmail.com" class="link-wipe inline-block text-primary">
          Get in touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
